    <!-- Unit Overview -->
    <section class="welcome-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass section-icon"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
        <p>The core concept is Strategic Evaluation of Emerging Technology. This unit requires students to move from general syllabus knowledge to the investigative research of a specific, pre-seen scenario. Key themes include System Interdependence, Contextual Application, and the Justification of Solutions in real-world emergencies or developments.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Syllabus Links -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark section-icon"></i> What You'll Learn</h2>
        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Understanding the System: Showing how the specific technology in the case study functions (AO1).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Syllabus Integration: Applying core concepts (e.g., Networks, Databases, ML) to the case study context (AO2).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Ethical & Social Impacts: Discussing impacts specific to the scenario, such as privacy in rescue operations or bias in automated systems (AO3).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Strategy Formulation: Evaluating and justifying strategies based on challenge questions and research (AO3).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Challenge Questions: Investigating the two specific challenges provided for SL.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

